# `__modname__` command group

`weld add command __modname__` generated this package. weld writes it once and
records every file in `weld.json`; it does not regenerate them, so your edits
survive later `weld add` commands.

## What it is

An independent root command group with no HTTP, configuration or database
dependency. `NewCommand` returns the `__modname__` command; with no subcommands
a bare `__name__ __modname__` shows help.

## How it is wired

`internal/app/__modname___command.go` registers the group through
`app.RegisterCommand`. Edit that file to pass business services into
`NewCommand`; `__modname__.NewCommand` is the stable factory to keep.

## Adding behaviour

Add subcommands in `command.go` with `cmd.AddCommand`. To reuse a business
module's logic, change `NewCommand` to accept the module's `Service`, call it
from a subcommand, and inject it in the registration file.
